module liveCellImagingDetection
module qPCRDetection

manifest PluronicF127
manifest PBS
manifest Fibronectin
manifest NIH3T3_Cells
manifest CellMedium
manifest TNF_Stimulus
manifest Trypsin_EDTA
manifest LysisBuffer
manifest CellsDirect_RTmix
manifest TaqMan_PrimerPool
manifest SuperScriptPlatinumTaq
manifest TEBuffer

instructions:

// ============================================================
// High-Throughput Microfluidic Single-Cell Analysis Pipeline
// for Studies of Signaling Dynamics
// Kellogg, Gomez-Sjoberg, Leyrat & Tay
// Nature Protocols Vol. 9 No. 7 (2014), pp. 1713-1726
// DOI: 10.1038/nprot.2014.120
//
// Platform: Two-layer PDMS cell culture chip (Gomez-Sjoberg
// et al., Anal. Chem. 2007) with 96 independently addressable
// 35-nL chambers (~1 x 1 mm x 35 um). Valve actuation by
// computer-controlled pneumatic solenoids (20-30 psi air).
// On-chip peristaltic pump (3-valve sequence) for metered
// feeding (~0.35 nL per pump cycle). Up to 16 reagent inputs
// via herringbone mixer. Example cell lines: NIH3T3 mouse
// fibroblasts and RAW264.7 macrophages. Stimulus: TNF-alpha.
//
// NOTE ON PLATFORM ABSTRACTION:
// This is a valve-actuated continuous-flow microfluidic chip,
// not a DMF/droplet electrode device. All `mix` steps here
// abstract pressure-driven fluid exchange events through
// microchannels and chamber volumes -- not electrode-driven
// droplet merging. `heat` steps model on-stage incubation
// under environmental control (37 C, 5% CO2, >95% humidity).
//
// NOTE ON FEEDING UNROLL:
// The protocol specifies 2-h feeding intervals with 30%
// chamber-volume exchange. Steps 35-36 call for overnight
// (~12 h) imaging + feeding before stimulation. Six feeding
// rounds (0h, 2h, 4h, 6h, 8h, 10h) are unrolled explicitly
// below (BioScript has no loop construct). Each feeding round
// dispenses fresh CellMedium and mixes for 1m to model one
// pump sequence replacing ~30% of chamber volume (30 cycles
// x ~0.35 nL = ~10.5 nL out of 35 nL).
//
// NOTE ON STIMULATION:
// TNF-alpha concentration range: 0.01-100 ng/mL (Step 38).
// Encoded here as a single representative input. Stimulus
// delivery modelled as pressure-driven flow replacing ~100%
// chamber volume (mode: full flush, not pump cycling).
// 10-min TNF pulse followed by medium washout (Step 40).
//
// NOTE ON qPCR THERMAL CYCLING:
// One-step RT-STA protocol (Step 54):
//   RT:          50 C for 15 min  (= 15m)
//   Taq activation: 95 C for 2 min (= 2m)
//   14 STA cycles: 95 C / 15 s + 60 C / 4 min each.
//     Cycle duration = 15s + 4m = 255s per cycle.
//     14 cycles = 14 x 255s = 3570s. Modelled as a single
//     heat step at 60 C for 3570s (dominant annealing phase).
//   Hold: 4 C (post-STA; modelled as heat at 4c for 5m).
//
// NOTE ON DURATION TOKENS:
// BioScript accepts `s` and `m` only. No `h` token. All
// overnight/multi-hour durations converted to minutes.
//   2 h feeding interval = 120m
//   Fibronectin chamber coating overnight = 720m
//   Imaging + feeding phase (~12 h) = unrolled into 6 x 120m
//   Cell growth and attachment (1 h) = 60m
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main             -- chip priming, surface treatment,
//                           cell loading, feeding, stimulation,
//                           live imaging, cell retrieval, RT-STA
//   BB2  qPCRPass         -- qPCRSignal > 0: valid Ct values;
//                           dispose all lysate/reaction products
//   BB3  qPCRFail         -- qPCRSignal <= 0: no amplification;
//                           drain all
//   BB4  finalCleanup     -- terminal: dispose QC signal
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 24-28: Chip surface treatment -- Pluronic blocking
// Pluronic F-127 (0.2% w/v in PBS) is flowed through all
// non-chamber surfaces for 1 h to block non-specific cell
// attachment to PDMS. Steps 24-29.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

primingPBS      = dispense 1 units of PBS
primingPluronic = dispense 1 units of PluronicF127
pluronicMix     = mix primingPBS with primingPluronic for 60m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 30: PBS wash -- remove Pluronic completely.
// Pluronic residue in chambers prevents fibronectin adhesion
// and downstream cell attachment. PBS flow for 30 min.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pbsWash1        = dispense 1 units of PBS
pluronicWashed  = mix pluronicMix with pbsWash1 for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 31: Fibronectin chamber coating.
// 100 ug/mL fibronectin in PBS flowed into non-chamber areas
// for 10 min to displace PBS, then valves opened to chambers.
// Chambers incubated overnight (720m) to promote ECM coating
// and rapid, reliable cell attachment (tested for 3T3 and
// RAW264.7 cell lines). Step 31.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

fibronectinSoln   = dispense 1 units of Fibronectin
fibronectinCoated = mix pluronicWashed with fibronectinSoln for 720m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 32-33: Cell loading.
// NIH3T3 fibroblast single-cell suspension (5e5 to 2e6
// cells/mL) pressurized with 5% CO2 at 3-5 psi and loaded
// through CellsIn port via PEEK tubing. Target: 150 fibroblasts
// per chamber (~80% confluence at experiment start).
// Cells adhere to fibronectin within minutes. Cell loading
// completes in 2-4 h (automated scripted seeding rounds).
// Attachment modelled as 60m incubation at 37 C.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

cellSuspension  = dispense 1 units of NIH3T3_Cells
loadedCells     = mix fibronectinCoated with cellSuspension for 60m
heat loadedCells at 37c for 60m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 34-37: Imaging and feeding -- 6 feeding rounds.
// 30% chamber volume replaced per round using on-chip
// peristaltic pump (30 cycles x ~0.35 nL/cycle = ~10.5 nL).
// Interval: every 2 h. Phase-contrast images acquired at each
// round to monitor cell growth (Step 37).
// 6 rounds unrolled covering ~12 h pre-stimulation imaging.
// Each feed: dispense fresh CellMedium, mix for 1m (pump seq).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Feed round 1 (t = 0 h, baseline)
feed1Medium  = dispense 1 units of CellMedium
fedCells1    = mix loadedCells with feed1Medium for 1m
heat fedCells1 at 37c for 120m

// Feed round 2 (t = 2 h)
feed2Medium  = dispense 1 units of CellMedium
fedCells2    = mix fedCells1 with feed2Medium for 1m
heat fedCells2 at 37c for 120m

// Feed round 3 (t = 4 h)
feed3Medium  = dispense 1 units of CellMedium
fedCells3    = mix fedCells2 with feed3Medium for 1m
heat fedCells3 at 37c for 120m

// Feed round 4 (t = 6 h)
feed4Medium  = dispense 1 units of CellMedium
fedCells4    = mix fedCells3 with feed4Medium for 1m
heat fedCells4 at 37c for 120m

// Feed round 5 (t = 8 h)
feed5Medium  = dispense 1 units of CellMedium
fedCells5    = mix fedCells4 with feed5Medium for 1m
heat fedCells5 at 37c for 120m

// Feed round 6 (t = 10 h)
feed6Medium  = dispense 1 units of CellMedium
fedCells6    = mix fedCells5 with feed6Medium for 1m
heat fedCells6 at 37c for 120m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 38-41: Cell stimulation experiment.
// TNF-alpha input prepared in CellMedium (0.01-100 ng/mL).
// Stimulus delivered by pressure-driven flow replacing full
// chamber volume (Step 40). 10-min TNF pulse (mode: full flush).
// Log stimulus timing for alignment with image data (Step 40
// critical step note). Delivery: PTFE tubing, 5% CO2 at 7 psi.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tnfStimulus     = dispense 1 units of TNF_Stimulus
stimulatedCells = mix fedCells6 with tnfStimulus for 10m

// TNF pulse washout: medium restored to chamber (Step 40).
// 60-min window captures NF-kB nuclear translocation
// dynamics (p65-dsRed nuclear intensity tracked over time).
washoutMedium   = dispense 1 units of CellMedium
postStimCells   = mix stimulatedCells with washoutMedium for 60m

// Additional stimulation cycles can be added here for pulse
// trains (e.g. TNF at t=0, 60, 120 min -- Step 40 example).
// Encoded as single representative 10-min TNF pulse.

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 32-43 (parallel): Live-cell fluorescence imaging.
// Automated time-lapse on inverted fluorescence microscope
// (Leica DMI6000B or Nikon Ti-E) with stage incubation
// (37 C, 5% CO2, >95% humidity). GFP and dsRed channels
// at 20x long-distance objective. 5-min frame interval.
// Nuclear p65-dsRed intensity / cytoplasmic p65-dsRed
// intensity quantified per cell per frame (Step 41).
// liveCellImagingDetection abstracts CellProfiler nuclear
// segmentation and NF-kB translocation quantification.
// Imaging runs for 300 min (5 h) post-stimulation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

imagingSignal = detect liveCellImagingDetection on postStimCells for 300m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 43: Fix/stain OR proceed to cell retrieval.
// Protocol Step 43: after stimulation, cells are either fixed
// for antibody endpoint staining OR retrieved live for gene
// expression analysis. Encoded here as live retrieval path.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 44-48: Cell retrieval for gene expression analysis.
// Trypsin-EDTA (0.05% w/v) delivered to each chamber.
// Cells detach within 1-3 min (~90% retrieval efficiency).
// Cells collected through ~10 cm PEEK tubing into 96-well
// plate wells pre-loaded with 5 uL lysis buffer (CellsDirect
// resuspension buffer + lysis enhancer). PBS wash between
// chambers prevents cross-contamination (Step 48).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

trypsinSoln     = dispense 1 units of Trypsin_EDTA
detachedCells   = mix postStimCells with trypsinSoln for 3m

lysisBuffer     = dispense 1 units of LysisBuffer
cellLysate      = mix detachedCells with lysisBuffer for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 49-54: One-step RT-STA (CellsDirect kit).
// Components per 10 uL reaction (Step 51):
//   5 uL 2x CellsDirect reaction mix (contains SuperScript III
//       / Platinum Taq mix)
//   1.5 uL TE buffer
//   2.5 uL 0.2x TaqMan primer pool (48 assays at 45 nM each)
//   1 uL SuperScript III / Platinum Taq mix
//   (+ 1 uL cell lysate added at Step 53)
//
// Thermal protocol (Step 54):
//   RT:           50 C, 15 min
//   Taq activation: 95 C, 2 min
//   14 STA cycles: [95 C / 15 s + 60 C / 4 min] x 14
//     = 3570 s total cycling (dominant 60 C annealing phase)
//   Hold: 4 C, 5 min (post-STA stabilisation)
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rtMix           = dispense 1 units of CellsDirect_RTmix
primerPool      = dispense 1 units of TaqMan_PrimerPool
superscriptTaq  = dispense 1 units of SuperScriptPlatinumTaq
teBuffer        = dispense 1 units of TEBuffer

// Assemble RT-STA reaction mix (Steps 50-52)
tmp1            = mix rtMix with primerPool for 5s
tmp2            = mix tmp1 with superscriptTaq for 5s
reactionMix     = mix tmp2 with teBuffer for 5s

// Add 1 uL cell lysate (Step 53)
rtStaReaction   = mix reactionMix with cellLysate for 5s

// RT step: reverse transcription at 50 C for 15 min
heat rtStaReaction at 50c for 15m

// Taq activation: 95 C for 2 min
heat rtStaReaction at 95c for 2m

// 14 STA cycles -- dominant 60 C annealing/extension phase
// 14 x (15s denaturation + 255s extension) = 3570s total
heat rtStaReaction at 60c for 3570s

// Post-STA hold at 4 C for 5 min
heat rtStaReaction at 4c for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 55: Dilute RT-STA product 1:3 with TE buffer.
// 22 uL TE added to 11 uL RT-STA product -> ~1:3 dilution
// (Step 55). Required before Fluidigm chip loading (Step 57).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

teDilutionBuffer = dispense 1 units of TEBuffer
dilutedProduct   = mix rtStaReaction with teDilutionBuffer for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 56-58: Fluidigm BioMark qPCR.
// 48.48 Dynamic Array IFC: 48 samples x 48 TaqMan assays
// = up to 9,216 simultaneous qPCR reactions.
// Assay wells (left half): 3.75 uL 2x assay loading reagent
//   + 3.75 uL each TaqMan assay (20x).
// Sample wells (right half): 3.4 uL diluted cDNA +
//   3.75 uL TaqMan PCR master mix + 0.4 uL sample loading
//   reagent. IFC controller MX primes the 48.48 Dynamic Array.
// qPCRDetection abstracts BioMark thermocycling and Ct
// calculation by Fluidigm Real-Time PCR Analysis software.
// Relative expression: 2^(Ct_gapdh - Ct_gene).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

qPCRSignal = detect qPCRDetection on dilutedProduct for 240m

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: qPCR QC gate
// Pass (BB2): qPCRSignal > 0 -> valid Ct values detected;
//             dispose all reaction products.
// Fail (BB3): qPCRSignal <= 0 -> no amplification (failed RT,
//             empty chamber, or IFC loading error); drain all.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (qPCRSignal > 0) {
    dispose dilutedProduct
    dispose cellLysate
    dispose imagingSignal
} else {
    drain dilutedProduct
    drain cellLysate
    drain imagingSignal
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose qPCR QC signal. Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose qPCRSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
